GPU painting through one WebGL2 context, CPU raster as fallback.

GLContext is reimplemented over a single WebGL2 context that the embedder
creates and registers (WebGL has no context sharing, so every GLContext is a
view over it). With no context registered, GL paths fail and painting stays on
the CPU. EGL is only used for the display object. Skia gets a GLES interface
over WebGL2 entry points: the version string is cut before "(WebGL" so Skia
picks GLES 3.0, and glGetInternalformativ is implemented over
getInternalformatParameter. Accelerated ImageBuffers flush without fences,
since producer and consumer share the one command stream. System font keywords
resolve to fontconfig sans-serif. Scroll animation follows the page setting.

